-- title:
--   Counting 𝔪-torsion in M/pM via base change to k
-- statement:
--   Let $T$ be a commutative ring and $M$ an abelian group carrying a $T$-module structure whose underlying $\mathbf Z$-module is finitely generated; let $\mathfrak m$ be an ideal of $T$, let $p$ be a prime and let $k$ be a field of characteristic $p$. Consider the quotient $M/\bigl(\operatorname{span}_T\{p\cdot 1_T\}\cdot M\bigr)$, that is, $M$ modulo the $T$-submodule generated by the products of elements of the ideal $(p)$ of $T$ with elements of $M$, and inside it the $\mathfrak m$-torsion submodule $\{x : t\,x = 0 \text{ for all } t \in \mathfrak m\}$. On the other side, for $t \in T$ let $t_k$ denote the $k$-linear endomorphism of $k \otimes_{\mathbf Z} M$ obtained by base change along $\mathbf Z \to k$ from the $\mathbf Z$-linear map $x \mapsto t\,x$ on $M$, and let $V = \bigcap_{t \in \mathfrak m} \ker t_k$, the infimum of the kernels of the $t_k$ over $t \in \mathfrak m$, a $k$-subspace of $k \otimes_{\mathbf Z} M$. The assertion is the equality of natural numbers $$\#\bigl(M/(p)M\bigr)[\mathfrak m] = p^{\,\dim_k V}.$$ Since the right-hand side is nonzero and `Nat.card` vanishes on infinite types, this also records that the $\mathfrak m$-torsion submodule is finite.
--
--   An elementary counting statement of commutative algebra: the $\mathfrak m$-torsion of $M/pM$ is an $\mathbf F_p$-vector space whose dimension is computed after the flat extension $\mathbf F_p \to k$, where it becomes the joint kernel of the operators of $\mathfrak m$ on $k \otimes_{\mathbf Z} M$. It is used in the comparison of the $\mathfrak m$-torsion of the quotient of an integral lattice attached to a modular curve with joint kernels of base-changed maps on cotangent spaces.
-- source:
--   https://github.com/anthropics/fermats-last-theorem/blob/aa2d8b34692b16c70f699536de0d8e75b9a3e9ef/Theorems/Thm_Module_card_torsionBySet_quotient_natCast_smul_top_eq_pow_finrank_iInf_ker_baseChange.lean

import Mathlib

